title: Ending_ZeusRoute
---
<<HideAll>>
<<StopMuzic 0.35>>
//CLOUD BG
<<Scene "Cloud 1">>
<<Scene "Cloud 4">>
<<Scene "Cloud 3">>
<<Scene "Cloud 2">>
<<PlayMusic Zeus_Theme>>
<<Act "Aelius" "Aelius 3_4s" "left" "bottom" #674ea7>>
<<Act "Zeus" "Zeus 3_4s" right bottom #bf9000>>
Zeus: Your mother… she must be something special.
Aelius: She is.
Zeus: If she’s anything like you, I don’t doubt it for a moment.
Zeus: And she...never told you anything about your father?
Aelius: It was a touchy subject. I didn’t push it.
Zeus: Ah...I see.
Zeus: Yes, having a godly parent can be, um... <i>taxing</i>.
Aelius: Doesn’t seem all that different from having normal parents, to be honest. Just a bit…

-> more emotional.
-> more fun.
-> more obnoxious.

Zeus: Hah! I can’t disagree with you there, Aelius.
Zeus: Regardless of what you think of us, we are <i>certainly</i> better off for having you.
Zeus: And I’m sure your mother will be better off once she’s seen you!

Aelius: She's...
Aelius: [Negative] Oh, gods. What if she’s not better off seeing me?
Zeus: Huh?
Aelius: [Negative] What if seeing me now only makes eternity in the Underworld more painful?
Zeus: What are you-
Aelius: [Negative] This is a mistake. We should turn back. Let's-
Zeus: AELIUS!
Zeus: Would you <i>please</i> just...
Zeus: ...
ZeusL I did not <i>intend</i> for my words to make you nervous.

Aelius: [Negative] You didn’t! I just-
Zeus: Aelius. Child. You must believe me when I say I understand the difficulties of family.
Zeus: It does not always feel like a blessing to have these connections.
Zeus: But if you’ve taught me and my family anything, it’s that avoiding problems only makes them worse with time.
Zeus: If you do not see her now, she will forever wonder how her child is doing without her.
Zeus: I am <i>sure</i> that your love and comfort will only be a blessing to her in the eons to come.
Zeus: AND! If I may be so bold...
Zeus: I think it will do you some good, too. To see her once again.
Aelius: [Negative] Zeus… Thank you.
Aelius: [Neutral] I may not know who my dad is...
Aelius: [Neutral] But I think I know who my family is.
Zeus: That is… quite the powerful sentiment.
Zeus: Your mother must be proud of you.
Aelius: ...Yeah.
Zeus: Go get 'em, champ.
<<HideAll>>
<<Act "Aelius" "Aelius 3_4s" "left" "bottom" #674ea7>>
Aelius: ...
Aelius: Hey, mom.
<<HideAll>>


<<LoadVNScene "Credits">>
===

title: Ending_HermesRoute
---
<<HideAll>>
<<StopMuzic 0.35>>
<<Act "Aelius" "Aelius 3_4s" "left" "bottom" #674ea7>>
<<Act "Hermes" "Hermes 3_4" "right" "bottom" #023020>>

//CLOUDS BG
<<Scene "Cloud 1">>
<<Scene "Cloud 4">>
<<Scene "Cloud 3">>
<<Scene "Cloud 2">>
<<PlayMusic Hermes_Theme>>
Hermes: It’ll be your first time down there, eh?
Aelius: Oh, yeah. Anything I should know?
Hermes: Meh, not really. Pretty gloomy, but I’m sure you guessed that.
Hermes: Just don’t go getting lost, I don’t want Hades getting ideas about opening up an Underworld diner with you as chef.
Aelius: [Smirk] I can’t imagine that’s a very good idea.
Hermes: Right? Like who would even go? Most of the Olympians avoid it there.
...
Hermes: ... You nervous?
Aelius: About what?
Hermes: Seeing your mom again. I can’t imagine it’ll be easy.
Aelius: ...
Aelius: [Negative] Yeah, I am.
Aelius: [Negative] It’s just… it’s still hard to believe she’s gone sometimes.
Aelius: [Negative] I’ll think to tell her something, and then I remember…
Hermes: I’m sorry, kid. I know that must be hard.
Aelius: [Negative] … It is. As much as I hate to show it.
Aelius: And now that I’ve been so caught up here… I realized I don't think about her every day.
Aelius: It feels like I’m betraying her, somehow.
Hermes: Hey, don’t think like that, Aelius.
Hermes: I’m sure she’d be happy to know you’re doing alright without her.
Hermes: You’re not a bad person for continuing on. It’s what she’d want.
Aelius: [Negative] ...
Aelius: Yeah, you're right. It's just hard to accept sometimes.
Hermes: Baby steps. Anything that’s worth doing is hard.
Aelius: [Negative] Do you think seeing her might be worse for me than just… well, not?
Hermes: [Neutral] Hm.
Hermes: I think it’ll be good, honestly.
Hermes: A way to get closure, to see that she’s doing well where she’s at.
Hermes: It’ll ease your mind, I’d bet.
Aelius: You really think so?
Hermes: Yeah. I’m not saying it’ll be easy, but it will help your grief in the long run.
Aelius: ...Yeah.
Aelius: [Smirk] Since when did you get so good at this emotion stuff?
Hermes: Oho! Teasing now? I really am rubbing off on you.
Hermes: Guess I’ll have to start calling you my kid.
Aelius: Haha! <i>Ole' Hermes</i>, already channeling his inner dad.
Hermes: Let's hope my knees don't start aching next.
...
Hermes: We're almost there.
Aelius: Wait, really?
Hermes: Mhm, the portal is just up ahead.
Aelius: ...
Aelius: Gods, I feel like an idiot. Being nervous over this.
Hermes: Don't be so hard on yourself. It'll be easier than you think, I can feel it.
Aelius: I hope you’re right.
Aelius: … I’m still excited, though.
Hermes: That’s good. I’m glad, Aelius.
Hermes: And I’ll be right there with ya.
Hermes: I ain’t planning on running away.
Aelius: [Positive] Thanks, Hermes.
Hermes: Here we are.
Hermes: [Positive] Take as much time as you need, we can head through whenever you're ready.
Aelius: ...
Aelius: I'm ready.
Hermes: Alright. You got this, kid.
<<HideAll>>
<<Act "Aelius" "Aelius 3_4s" "left" "bottom" #674ea7>>
Aelius: ... Woah.
<<Act "Hermes" "Hermes 3_4" "right" "bottom" #023020>>
Hermes: Crazy here, eh? As I said – don’t mind the doom and gloom, you’ll get used to it.
A figure appears in the distance.
Aelius: Is that...?
Hermes: Yeah, yeah it is.
Hermes: Go on, kid. I'll be here if you need me.
<<Hide Hermes>>
Aelius: ...
Aelius: [Positive] Hey, mom.
<<HideAll>>

<<LoadVNScene "Credits">>
===

title: Ending_HephaestusRoute
---
<<Act "Aelius" "Aelius 3_4s" "left" "bottom" #674ea7>>
<<Act "Hephaestus" "Hephaestus" "right" "bottom" #FF8C00>>
//CLOUDS BG
<<Scene "Cloud 1">>
<<Scene "Cloud 4">>
<<Scene "Cloud 3">>
<<Scene "Cloud 2">>
<<StopMuzic 0.35>>
<<PlayMusic Hephaestus_Theme>>
Hephaestus: I'm not the best at expressing myself.
Hephaestus: Although I’m sure that’s obvious.
Aelius: [Positive] I think you do okay.
Hephaestus: You don’t have to flatter me.
Hephaestus: But thank you.
Hephaestus: What I wanted to say is that you’ve been someone that I can talk to.
Hephaestus: And I want you to know that you can talk to me.
Hephaestus: You must be nervous; seeing your mom again is a big deal.
Hephaestus: If you need it, I’ll be here. It’s what a father ought to do.
-> I'm just not sure what I'm going to say.
    Aelius: Like, what if I get there and I can't say anything, and I just stand there?
    Aelius: Or if I say the wrong thing and I mess everything up?
    Hephaestus: Aelius...
    Aelius: Is it wrong that I don’t have anything to say?
    Hephaestus: Aelius. Not many mortals could do what you’ve done in just a week.
    Hephaestus: Nor could many gods.
    Hephaestus: You have the strength and wisdom of Olympus in you, remember that.
    Aelius: Yes… I will. Thank you.
    Hephaestus: When the time comes, you’ll know what to say.
    Aelius: Alright… alright. I’m ready.
-> Thank you, but I’m more excited than anything.
    Aelius: I've missed her a lot.
    Aelius: There's so much I’ve wanted to say.
    Hephaestus: I’m glad.
    Aelius: Hephaestus…
    Hephaestus: Yes?
    Aelius: Is it wrong that I’m not more sad?
    Hephaestus: Of course not.
    Hephaestus: You’re seeing her again after all.
    Hephaestus: And I know, seeing someone you love after a long time apart is the best feeling in the world.
    Aelius: [Positive] Yeah, I think you're right.
    Hephaestus: Besides, death isn’t like how you mortals imagine it.
    Hephaestus: Her soul remains, and I’m sure this won’t be the last time you see her.
-> It’s been so long, what if I’m making the wrong choice?
    Hephaestus: What do you mean?
    Aelius: I mean, what's it been like for her in the Underworld?
    Aelius: What if she doesn’t want to see me?
    Aelius: What if she never wanted me to get mixed up with the gods?
    Hephaestus: Aelius. It’s worth it to see a loved one again, even if it's a risk.
    Hephaestus: That's what you helped me to understand.
    Hephaestus: And she raised an intelligent and resourceful child. An excellent craftsperson.
    Hephaestus: She’ll want to see how you’ve grown, and you were more than prepared to meet the gods.
    Hephaestus: If she wanted to protect you, she did the best job she could.
    Aelius: Alright... alright. I'm ready.

Hephaestus: Before you step through the portal, one last thing.
Hephaestus: I'm proud of you.
Hephaestus: And so is Aphrodite, and I’m sure that Hestia is, too.
Aelius: Oh… Thank you so much.
Hephaestus: I don’t know what you will see in the Underworld.
Hephaestus: But I know your mother will be proud of you as well.
Aelius: [Positive] And I am proud of you too, Hephaestus.
Aelius: [Positive] You and the rest of the Olympians are my family now.
Aelius: [Positive] Even if I don’t know who my dad is.
Hephaestus: Aphrodite will be delighted to hear that.
Hephaestus: It- It means a lot to me as well…
Aelius: [Positive] Thank you for coming with me.
Hephaestus: Of course. I’ll be right outside.
Aelius: [Positive] Alright, I am ready.
<<Hide Hephaestus>>
Aelius: ...
Aelius: [Positive] Hey, mom.


<<LoadVNScene "Credits">>
===

title: Ending_HestiaRoute
---
<<HideAll>>
<<Act "Aelius" "Aelius 3_4s" "left" "bottom" #674ea7>>
<<Act "Hestia" "Hestia 3_4s" "right" "bottom" #e06666>>
//CLOUDS BG
Hestia: We will be headed to Hades’ realm, Aelius. I’m… sure it’s probably not what you had in mind when reuniting with your mother.
Aelius: Well, I’m not sure how I was picturing the Underworld – I guess just dark and dreary.
Hestia: That about sums his territory up, though he is trying to improve that. Something about needing engineers…
Hestia: I agree that he does need to spruce this place up a bit, though. Maybe you’d have some ideas for him?
Aelius: Maybe later down the line, for now I’m just trying to hold it all together right now.
Hestia: *<i>Soft chuckle.</i>*
Hestia: Let me guide you then so you don’t have to think about that part at all. I’ve been down there a few times before when Zeus has allowed it.
Aelius: You’ve been down there before?
Hestia: Yes, I’ve been down there on a… ‘business trip,’ you could say.
Aelius: What was it about? I’m sure it was pretty important if you were allowed to leave Olympus.
Hestia: Hades and I were considering opening an establishment down there soon, but I’m not sure what will happen with that.
Hestia: But we’re not here for that, we’re here for you. How are you feeling about all this?
Aelius: I don’t know, I’m feeling a whole lotta everything at the moment.
Aelius: Happy, sad, anxious… everything just feels surreal.
Hestia: We can take as much time as you need, there’s no rush.
Hestia: I will be with you every step of the way.
Aelius: Thanks, Hestia.
Aelius: I think I'm ready now.
//BLACK BG
Hestia: We’ve made it down to Hades’ realm, lots of dark and more darkness to behold.
Aelius: … We’ve really made it.
Hestia: We’ve made it to the spot Hades said to be…
A figure appears in the distance.
Aelius: Is- is that...?
Hestia: Yes dear, your mother is here.
Aelius: *<i>Sniffle</i>*
Hestia: Go, see her. I will be here whenever you might need me.
<<Hide Hestia>>
Aelius: ...
Aelius: [Positive] Hey, mom.



<<LoadVNScene "Credits">>
===
